# SPA FALLBACK — REQUIRED FOR STEP 1's URL ROUTING TO WORK ON REFRESH.
#
# THE GAP THIS FIXES: without this file, requesting /cost-architecture
# directly (a hard refresh, a bookmark, a shared link someone clicks) has
# no matching file for Cloudflare Pages to serve, and returns a 404 - even
# though the route is completely valid inside the app. This rule tells
# Cloudflare: for any path that doesn't match a real file (a .js, .css, an
# image), serve index.html instead, with a 200 status (not a redirect) so
# the browser's address bar keeps the original URL and React can read it
# to open the right module.
#
# Real static assets (already-existing files) are matched and served
# normally BEFORE this catch-all rule is ever reached - this does not
# change how any existing file on the site is served.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
